# Coarse-grained (spheres and gaussians) test structure for the MVS annotation selectors.
#
# Derived from PDB-IHM entry PDBDEV_00000017 (PDB 8ZZH, "Molecular architecture of the major membrane ring component, Pom152,
# of the yeast nuclear pore complex"), downloaded from https://pdb-ihm.org/cif/pdbdev_00000017.cif and trimmed to the categories
# needed to load the coarse model. Only chain A (entity 1, 882 spheres) is the original data. No small PDB-IHM entry has gaussian
# objects, so chains B-D are generated:
#   B: entity 1, gaussian objects made from the spheres of A (mean = sphere center + 100 A in x, isotropic covariance from the radius)
#   C: entity 2 (a copy of entity 1), the spheres of A shifted by -100 A in x
#   D: entity 2, gaussian objects made like those of B, shifted by -100 A in x
# It is test data, not a valid model of the complex.
data_8ZZH_COARSE_TEST
_entry.id 8ZZH_COARSE_TEST
#
loop_
_entity.id
_entity.type
_entity.src_method
_entity.pdbx_description
1 polymer man pom152
2 polymer man 'pom152 copy'
#
loop_
_struct_asym.id
_struct_asym.entity_id
_struct_asym.details
A 1 pom152
B 1 'pom152 gaussians'
C 2 'pom152 copy'
D 2 'pom152 copy gaussians'
#
loop_
_entity_poly.entity_id
_entity_poly.type
1 polypeptide(L)
2 polypeptide(L)
